! =============================================================================
! AMPS Earth validation C9: PAMELA public-data global-shell cutoff validation
!
! Scientific observable
! ---------------------
! Adriani et al. (2016) Supporting Information Table S1 reports the magnitude
! of the proton cutoff AACGM latitude for seven rigidity bins.  Each timestamp
! is the middle of one 94-minute PAMELA interval.  C9 does not attempt to
! reconstruct the proprietary Resurs-DK1 attitude/ephemeris.  Instead, it makes
! a public-data global-shell comparison at PAMELA's representative altitude:
!
!   * one 475-km geodetic shell;
!   * vertically incident protons;
!   * IGRF + T05/TS05 driven by the bundled five-minute C9 driver;
!   * PENUMBRA_SCAN, retaining Rc_lower, Rc_effective, and Rc_upper;
!   * an additional exact-rigidity access-state product at the seven PAMELA
!     geometric-center rigidities;
!   * the primary modeled cutoff is the longitude-averaged T=0.5 boundary,
!     evaluated over the same configured geodetic latitude band as the GRIDDED
!     DIRECT_ACCESS product and then converted to AACGM in each hemisphere.
!
! The Python runner copies this template into every snapshot directory and
! changes only named directives (EPOCH, DRIVER_FILE, scan count/resolution,
! rigidity bracket, and numerical controls).  The generated input is archived
! with every result so the comparison is reproducible.
! =============================================================================

#CALCULATION_MODE
CALC_TARGET             CUTOFF_RIGIDITY
FIELD_EVAL_METHOD       GRIDLESS

#CUTOFF_RIGIDITY
! Default bracket 0.30-1.35 GV for protons.  The corresponding kinetic-energy
! limits are written explicitly because the AMPS cutoff parser accepts energy.
CUTOFF_EMIN             46.7936514838217
CUTOFF_EMAX             705.763955063706
CUTOFF_MAX_PARTICLES    1
CUTOFF_NENERGY          50
CUTOFF_SAMPLING         VERTICAL
CUTOFF_SEARCH_ALGORITHM PENUMBRA_SCAN
CUTOFF_UPPER_SCAN_N     160
CUTOFF_SCAN_SPACING     LINEAR
! During PENUMBRA_SCAN a non-empty rigidity list requests an additional
! long-form access-state file at these exact values. The complete 160-node scan
! and Rc_lower/Rc_effective/Rc_upper outputs are unchanged. C9 uses the companion
! states to calculate the same PAMELA_T50 observable as the Mode3D branches.
CUTOFF_RIGIDITY_LIST_GV 0.423556372,0.498397432,0.587877538,0.692820323,0.817006732,0.962081078,1.131017241
! GRIDLESS does not execute RIGIDITY_LIST, so these directives do not reduce
! the C++ full-shell work. The runner nevertheless uses the same values to filter
! the companion access rows before AACGM/T50 fitting, keeping the scientific
! latitude domain identical to GRIDDED DIRECT_ACCESS and GRIDDED FULL_SCAN.
CUTOFF_ACCESS_ABS_LAT_MIN 35.0
CUTOFF_ACCESS_ABS_LAT_MAX 75.0
CUTOFF_TRACE_POLICY     ACCURATE
CUTOFF_BACKTRACE_CHARGE REVERSED
CUTOFF_TRACE_LIMIT_POLICY FORBIDDEN
CUTOFF_MAX_TRAJ_TIME    20.0

#PARTICLE_SPECIES
SPECIES                 PROTON
CHARGE                  1
MASS_AMU                1.007276466621

#BACKGROUND_FIELD
! The driver table is sampled once at EPOCH for each standalone snapshot run.
! The runner uses the checksum-verified driver bundled under C9/data by default.
FIELD_MODEL             T05
EPOCH                   2006-12-15T03:03:00
DRIVER_FILE             ts05_driver.txt
! Static values are parser-safe fallbacks only.  A loaded driver overrides them.
DST                     -100.0
PDYN                    4.0
IMF_BX                  0.0
IMF_BY                  0.0
IMF_BZ                  -5.0
SW_VX                   -450.0
SW_N                    5.0
T05_W1                  0.0
T05_W2                  0.0
T05_W3                  0.0
T05_W4                  0.0
T05_W5                  0.0
T05_W6                  0.0

#DOMAIN_BOUNDARY
! Bare lengths are kilometers.  +/-25 Re is large enough for the empirical
! magnetosphere used by this event-level access calculation.
DOMAIN_X_MIN            -159280.0
DOMAIN_X_MAX             159280.0
DOMAIN_Y_MIN            -159280.0
DOMAIN_Y_MAX             159280.0
DOMAIN_Z_MIN            -159280.0
DOMAIN_Z_MAX             159280.0
R_INNER                  6371.2

#SPECTRUM
! Required by the common parser; not used by cutoff-rigidity tracing.
SPECTRUM_TYPE           POWER_LAW
SPEC_J0                 1.0
SPEC_GAMMA              2.0
SPEC_E0                 1000.0
SPEC_EMIN               1.0
SPEC_EMAX               2000.0

#OUTPUT_DOMAIN
! Full geographic shell.  The runner transforms these grid points to AACGM in
! postprocessing at the exact snapshot epoch.  SHELL_GEOMETRY=GEODETIC follows
! the current Earth cutoff-test convention.
OUTPUT_MODE             SHELLS
SHELL_COUNT             1
SHELL_ALTS_KM           475.0
SHELL_LON_RES_DEG       30.0
SHELL_LAT_RES_DEG       2.0
SHELL_GEOMETRY          GEODETIC

#OUTPUT_OPTIONS
OUTPUT_COORDS           GEO

#NUMERICAL
DT_TRACE                0.2
ADAPTIVE_DT             T
MAX_STEPS               500000
MAX_TRACE_TIME          20.0
MAX_TRACE_DISTANCE      400.0
TRAP_DETECTION          T

!#END
